or Research on Cancer</publisher-name><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>184</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Surveillance Epidemiology and End Results</collab></person-group><source>Summary Staging Manual 2000: Codes and Coding Instructions</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Bethesda: National Cancer Institute</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Public Health Division</collab></person-group><source>NSW Clinical Cancer Data Collection for Outcomes and Quality</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Sydney: NSW Health Department</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Commission on Cancer</collab></person-group><article-title>National Cancer Data Base</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.facs.org/cancder/ncdb/indexhtml"/></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schneider</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name><name><surname>Malin</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kahn</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Emanuel</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Epstein</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Developing a system to assess the quality of cancer care: ASCO's national initiative on cancer care quality</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>2004</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>2985</fpage><lpage>2991</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15284249</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1200/JCO.2004.09.087</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walter</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name